      "writtenOn": "2021-03-31T16:40:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hard reset is limited to a pretty narrow set of states, according to Table 6-65 note 1, so I\u0027m not sure we could rationalize that one without getting some WG feedback first. \n\nI don\u0027t want to leave us in a state of Vconn on because that gives us the false impression that we are the sole port allowed to initiate SOP\u0027 messages, and will lead to confusion on any SOP\u0027 transactions if the partner also believes as such.  \n\nI am open to any other suggestions that get us into a good state here.  Following spec exactly and soft resetting doesn\u0027t solve the issue unless we add in qualifiers to ensure we\u0027re not going to muddy the SOP\u0027 waters. \n\nDo we have a branching path for \"does it work with TCPMv1\"?  This particular charger was shipped with some TCPMv1 chromebooks from what I gather, which would never have noticed the issue due to never bothering to cable probe/Vconn swap/run PD 3.0.",
      "parentUuid": "3b910d02_2c70594c",
      "revId": "559247e7058cf344064e762b69d311b69be6b957",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
